NOTICE
======

GlassBar theme system
---------------------

GlassBar's file-defined theme system is *inspired by* the skin architecture of
Rainmeter (a desktop customization tool) in the general sense that a theme is a
folder containing a plain-text definition plus its own assets, with inherited
and variable-substituted values.

It is an INDEPENDENT IMPLEMENTATION written for GlassBar. No Rainmeter source
code, plugin headers, bundled skins, skin files, INI files, or documentation
text were copied, adapted, or consulted as a source of implementation.

Rainmeter is licensed under the GNU General Public License v2.0 (GPL-2.0).
GlassBar is not GPL-licensed and is not derived from Rainmeter; this theme
system shares no code or assets with it. The names, file layout and behaviour
here are GlassBar's own design, chosen to fit GlassBar's existing settings
model.

The theme model deliberately stops at restyling the widgets GlassBar already
ships: colours, geometry, typography, opacity, and which widgets are shown and
in what order. It contains no expression, measure or meter language, and no
plugin or extension mechanism.
